# Rebuild and restart when the code is ready

When an implementation is finished and the code is ready to build, run `rebuild-and-restart.sh` from the repo root with Git Bash before reporting it done. That script stops the servers, rebuilds, refreshes `chaos.conf`, and starts the servers.

Never run this script if the only files you changed are `.lua` files. Lua scripts load without a rebuild, so a Lua-only change is finished once the files are saved.

Do not run it for unfinished work, a change you expect to fail the build, or a task that does not need a rebuild (docs, rules, or questions only).

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" "C:/AzerothCore/rebuild-and-restart.sh"
```

```text
❌ Run the script while the change is still incomplete
❌ Run the script when the only changes are .lua files
❌ cmake, or a rebuild by hand instead of the script
✅ Run the script once the change is ready to compile
✅ Skip the script when every changed file ends in .lua
```

If the script fails, stop. Do not start the servers another way.
